            "reviewBody": "Awesome for when you go camping &amp; no mess &amp; fuss!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "frankschick"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Fabulous idea! I gave it five stars just for the ease of the recipe alone! Fast prep and cleanup too! I have made these plain with salt and pepper, but I have also made them with peppers, chopped onions, once with chopped bacon and shredded cheese. There really is no limit and I love that you can make each muffin cup egg a different version, so everyone gets one that they like!",
            "datePublished": "2013-06-01T07:31:52.540Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "HappyGrandma"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great fun plus really good! If scrambled plus shredded cheese, I fill 3 muffin cups 2/3 full from 2 eggs. Light, tender &amp; cute! Hubby likes his sunny side up &amp; comes out perfect.",
            "datePublished": "2014-04-13T17:08:22.800Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "EdFenster"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is also a great idea if you are not grilling. I used it to make mini-omelets by beating eggs will a little milk and seasoning with salt and pepper. Into each muffin cup I put some shredded cheddar and onion. I filled each cup to about a quarter inch from the top. At 350 F, they took 25 minutes. When they puff up a little past the top, they are done. If you spray the pan first with cooking spray, they pop right out.",
            "datePublished": "2018-07-11T21:19:04.337Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lillian"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This worked out very nicely! Its a great way to make eggs while camping! The only problem I had was that the eggs stuck to the muffin pan even though I oiled it! I grilled mine on the lowest setting(450 degrees on the grill thermometer) because I was worried my muffin pan would burn. It didn't burn at that temp. and the eggs were perfectly cooked in 5 minutes. I made the eggs a few ways! Scrambled with bacon bits and cheese... sunnyside up with cheese and a slice of ham forming a cup... and just regular sunnyside up with cheese. The scrambled eggs bubbled over the edge of the pan for some reason, so I won't do that next time. The ham one was my favorite!",
            "datePublished": "2013-06-20T16:59:13.207Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Alisha Bennett"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Fun with Food!!! This recipe was delicious and fun to make. I love that each one can be personalized with herbs or veggies/cheese. Just be careful not to overfill with goodies. These did take a bit longer than the recipe states; perhaps next time warming the eggs up to room temperature would help.",
            "datePublished": "2014-12-03T11:10:47.353Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Baking Nana"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I am giving this 5 stars because it is a great idea &amp; fun for the kids and adults alike. Obviously if you want a firm set egg, cook longer. The eggs slide right out of the muffin tins. All I added was a little salt and pepper to each egg. Next time I think I will scramble the eggs. Thanks for posting this great idea.",
            "datePublished": "2016-07-04T20:59:52.910Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "DEMOREO"
            },
            "reviewBody": "It was very fun to grill eggs for breakfast at home. The eggs did not cook all the way on the top of our scrambled eggs so I had to flip them. I added a piece of cooked bacon on the top and some cheese to melt. Very good and fun.",
            "datePublished": "2005-07-01T07:23:17.280Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Hershey Recipes"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I was quite excited to try this. it was easy, and didn't require much on my end. but it gave a new taste that was quite enjoyable.\n\nI'm excited to try new variations with this. I just used S&amp;P along with some garlic powder. MMMMM :)",
            "datePublished": "2014-06-03T09:31:26.850Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MattOlay V-H"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Did this for our camping trip and it turned out well.\r\n I used an aluminum muffin pan and greased it very well. I like mine crispy so I had placed half of the pan directly on the fire a little longer.",
            "datePublished": "2013-06-25T08:01:52.410Z"
